<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Nov oil output fell 0.88 pct vs yr ago.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Nov oil output fell 0.88 pct vs yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador produced an average of 381,694 barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in November, down 0.88 percent from the same month last year, an official said Thursday.</p>
<p>An official from the official Petroleum National Direction, who asked not to be named, said that in November 1995 the country produced an average of 385,096 bpd.</p>
<p>Ecuador's average production in the first 11 months was 384,245 bpd, he added, without giving a comparative figure for 1995.</p>
<p>Oil production in Ecuador last year was an average of 386,706 bpd.</p>
<p>In October 1996, oil production was 387,374 bpd.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
